                        "title":  "Kampala History",
                        "answer":  "Kampala is the capital of Uganda and has deep historical connections to the Kingdom of Buganda. Its modern urban development includes the establishment of a colonial fort at Old Kampala in 1890. Kampala subsequently grew as a centre of commerce and administration. It received city status on 28 September 1962, shortly before Uganda gained independence on 9 October 1962.",
